<title>BRAZIL: Brazil coffee crop to fall in 1997/98 - agronomist.</title>
<headline>Brazil coffee crop to fall in 1997/98 - agronomist.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian coffee production should drop in 1997/98 before bouncing back the following year, said a coffee agronomist from the Agricultural Economics Institute of the Sao Paulo Agricultural Secretariat.</p>
<p>&quot;Coffee production next year will likely be 20 percent below this year,&quot; said Luiz Moricochi.</p>
<p>&quot;The 1995/96 crop was 12.6 60-kg million bags after the frosts and the drought. This year's harvest was double that and in 1997 there will be a 20 percent fall. But in 1998 I would say that the crop will be at least 30 million bags,&quot; he added.</p>
</text>
